  "body": "## Associated User Story\r\n\r\nAs an officer I want to be able to see all members (and which are active with at least 7 points) and all of their information from the member intake so I can keep track who is still present in the org and who to contact to get their attendance up.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance Criteria\r\n\r\n\r\n### Officers can see all members, their active status, and their intake information in one place\r\n\r\n- **Sunny:**An officer opens the member tracker and sees every member with their point total, an active/inactive status (active = at least 7 points), and their intake info (name, TAMU email, etc.). Members with 7 or more points show as active, and the rest show as inactive so officers know who to contact.\r\n- **Rainy:** The member data fails to load, or a member has missing intake info. The officer sees a clear \"try again\" message instead of a blank page, and any member with blank fields still appears with those fields marked as missing.\r\n\r\n**Definition of Done** -\r\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\r\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\r\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\r\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
